Error [E1113]: `frozen` cannot be assigned; it was frozen at `freeze(...)` at byte 87
  --> tests/ui/frozen_write.jet:8:12
    |
  8 |     frozen.value = 2
    |            ^^^^^
 Why: `freeze(...)` creates a deeply immutable owned snapshot so a task can read it without a race. A write through any field or index would change that snapshot.
 Fix: create a new value, freeze a new snapshot, or use `Shared`/`Cell` when shared mutation is intentional

Error [E0205]: cannot edit `value` — `frozen` does not have the write-access marker `&`
  --> tests/ui/frozen_write.jet:8:12
    |
  8 |     frozen.value = 2
    |            ^^^^^
 Why: editing a field requires the write-access marker `&` on the owning place
 Fix: declare it with `frozen := ...` to give it write access
